menu "Coordinator"


    config COORDINATOR_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Coordinator Task Stack Size"
        default 4096

    config COORDINATOR_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Coordinator Task Priority"
        default 5

    config COORDINATOR_TASK_NAME
        string "Coordinator Task Name"
        default "COORDINATOR_TASK"

    config COORDINATOR_MAX_HEATING_PROFILE_STEPS
        int "Max heating profile steps"
        default 20

    config COORDINATOR_MAX_PROFILES_STORED
        int "Max number of stored profiles"
        default 5

    config COORDINATOR_PID_TICK_INTERVAL_MS
        int "PID control loop tick interval (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 100 10000
        help
            How often the PID control loop runs (computes target temp,
            runs PID, and sends power to the heater). 1000 ms = 1 Hz.

    config COORDINATOR_SENSOR_AGGREGATE_STALE_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Maximum sensor aggregate age (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 1000 60000
        help
            Maximum age of a successful physical sensor sample accepted into
            the temperature aggregate. If fewer than the required sensor
            quorum are fresh, heating is inhibited and the active profile is
            paused.

    config COORDINATOR_SENSOR_RECOVERY_VALID_AGGREGATES
        int "Consecutive valid aggregates before sensor recovery"
        default 3
        range 1 20
        help
            Number of consecutive valid aggregate updates required before the
            coordinator may release the recoverable sensor-data inhibit.

    config COORDINATOR_SENSOR_AUTO_RECOVERY
        bool "Automatically recover from sensor-data inhibit"
        default y
        help
            Permit the coordinator to release the recoverable sensor-data
            inhibit after the configured valid aggregate count. Permanent
            hardware inhibits are never cleared by this setting.

    config COORDINATOR_PROFILE_COMPLETE_TEMP_C
        int "Temperature threshold for profile completion (C)"
        default 40
        range 20 100
        help
            The profile is considered complete when the cooldown stage
            has been reached AND the measured temperature drops below
            this value.

    config COORDINATOR_OVERSHOOT_THRESHOLD_C
        int "Maximum allowed overshoot above setpoint (C)"
        default 20
        range 5 100
        help
            If the measured temperature exceeds the current setpoint by
            more than this value, the program is emergency-stopped and
            the heater is cut. Protects against runaway temperatures.

            This is a hard RUNAWAY guard, not a quality limit — it must sit
            ABOVE the worst transient overshoot at the top of a ramp or it
            will nuisance-trip on normal arrival. 20 C suits a <=200 C
            composite-curing furnace; quality overshoot (keeping the arrival
            peak within a few C) is a PID-tuning job (Kd), not this threshold.

    config COORDINATOR_RAMP_EASE_BAND_C
        int "Ramp soft-landing band before hold (C)"
        default 6
        range 0 50
        help
            Width of the soft-landing zone at the TOP of a heating ramp. Over
            the last this-many degrees before the stage target, the commanded
            setpoint rate is tapered smoothly to zero instead of holding the
            full ramp rate right up to the hand-over to the HOLDING stage.

            WHY: at a sharp ramp->hold corner the chamber is still rising at the
            full ramp rate AND the integrator is wound up for "climbing" power,
            so the chamber coasts past the target (the classic ramp->hold
            overshoot) and then takes a minute or two to settle as the
            integrator unwinds. Tapering the final approach lets the controller
            reach hold power BEFORE the corner, so there is little surplus left
            to coast on.

            Tuning: 0 disables it (pure linear ramp = original behaviour).
            Widen it if a stubborn overshoot remains; narrow it if the final
            approach feels sluggish. Complements PID Kd (which brakes on rise
            rate) — this reshapes the setpoint so there is less to brake. Keep
            it at or below COORDINATOR_HOLD_BAND_C so the eased approach stays
            well inside the hold alarm band.

    config COORDINATOR_HANDOVER_TOLERANCE_X10
        int "Ramp->hold handover tolerance, tenths C (5 = 0.5 C)"
        default 5
        range 0 50
        help
            How close to the stage target the chamber must reach before a
            HEATING stage hands over to its HOLDING phase, in TENTHS of a degree
            C (5 = 0.5 C). Stored x10 so menuconfig stays integer-only.

            WHY SEPARATE FROM NEXTION_TEMP_TOLERANCE_C: that shared tolerance is
            whole-degree and also governs cooling-stage advance, stage phase
            detection and program validation, so it cannot be tightened just for
            the hand-over. This knob controls ONLY the heating->hold advance.

            EFFECT: the soft-landing ramp (COORDINATOR_RAMP_EASE_BAND_C) tapers
            the setpoint to the target, but the hand-over fires when the chamber
            reaches target - this_tolerance. With the old shared 2 C the hand-over
            happened 2 C early, so the chamber climbed that last 2 C under a hard
            proportional push and coasted past (overshoot) then dipped. A small
            value (0.5 C) lets the chamber track the eased ramp almost to the
            target and arrive gently. 0 = hand over only on reaching target
            exactly; widen it if a furnace has steady ramp lag and would
            otherwise never get close enough to advance.

    config COORDINATOR_STALL_CHECK_MS
        int "Heating stall detection window (ms)"
        default 300000
        range 60000 600000
        help
            During HEATING, if the measured temperature has not risen by
            at least the expected amount (based on the setpoint ramp) within
            this time window, the program is paused and a stall error is
            reported.  Default is 300000 ms (5 minutes). A stalled heater
            fails OFF (not dangerous), so a longer window trades slower
            detection for fewer nuisance pauses on transient lag.

    config COORDINATOR_STALL_MIN_LAG_C
        int "Heating stall minimum lag below setpoint (C)"
        default 5
        range 0 100
        help
            A stall is only declared when the chamber is at least this many
            degrees BELOW the moving setpoint (i.e. genuinely behind), in
            addition to failing the rate check below. This gate prevents a
            false stall when the chamber has overshot and the PID has
            correctly cut power: the temperature goes flat while the setpoint
            keeps climbing, but we are ahead, not stalled.

    config COORDINATOR_STALL_RATE_FRACTION_PCT
        int "Heating stall rate fraction (% of programmed ramp)"
        default 50
        range 0 100
        help
            Within the stall window, the chamber must achieve at least this
            fraction of the programmed ramp rise. Achieving less (while also
            behind by COORDINATOR_STALL_MIN_LAG_C) declares a stall. Default
            50 % = "rising at less than half the programmed rate".

    config COORDINATOR_HOLD_BAND_C
        int "Hold-phase deviation alarm band (C)"
        default 4
        range 1 100
        help
            During a HOLDING (dwell) phase, if the chamber stays more than
            this many degrees away from the target (above OR below) for
            COORDINATOR_HOLD_VIOLATION_MS, the program is paused and a
            hold-deviation error is reported so a worker can intervene.
            4 C is a conservative alarm for a prepreg cure dwell; tighten
            toward 2-3 C once measured dwell ripple confirms the headroom.
            (The control target is tighter than the alarm band — keep this
            generous to avoid nuisance pauses on settling. This is an ALARM
            band, not the control setpoint: it must sit above the steady
            hold ripple or it will trip on normal dwell.)

    config COORDINATOR_HOLD_VIOLATION_MS
        int "Hold-phase deviation sustain time before pause (ms)"
        default 300000
        range 10000 600000
        help
            How long the chamber must remain continuously outside
            COORDINATOR_HOLD_BAND_C before a hold-deviation pause is raised.
            The sustain timer resets as soon as the chamber re-enters the
            band, so brief settling excursions do not trip it. Default
            300000 ms (5 minutes) — hold stages run for hours, so a longer
            sustain absorbs load/door disturbances. The over-temperature
            direction is still caught quickly by the overshoot guard
            (COORDINATOR_OVERSHOOT_THRESHOLD_C), so this can be generous
            without risking a runaway during a long hold.

    config COORDINATOR_COMPONENT_ID
        int "Coordinator Component ID"
        default 4
        help
            Unique identifier for the Coordinator component used by the health monitor.

    config COORDINATOR_HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Coordinator Heartbeat Timeout (ms)"
        default 5000
        help
            Maximum time between heartbeats before the health monitor considers the coordinator unhealthy.

endmenu
